  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find $\\alpha $ we use $arctan.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\alpha  & =0.70 \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\alpha ) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0.70) \\\\ \\alpha  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0.70)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using a calculator, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0.70) \\\\  & =(34.992\\,0…)^{∘} \\\\  & ≈{35.0}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
